    title: "Anthropic’s $15 Billion Credit Line Sets Stage for IPO",
    summary: "Anthropic’s anticipated IPO could kick off a busy fall for tech listings after SpaceX dominated the market this summer. Rainmaker Securities co-founder and Managing Director Greg Martin discusses why Anthropic’s planned $15 billion revolving credit facility strengthens its position ahead of a potential offering. He also shares how its rapid growth could support a valuation above SpaceX’s at IPO and why a successful debut could “open the floodgates” for companies including Oura, neoclouds and other long-awaited tech listings. He joins Bloomberg’s Lisa Mateo on \"Bloomberg Tech.\"",
